  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance for Banking &amp; Financial Services - Uruguay</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In an initial engagement, OTAs Banking &amp; Financial Services Team placed a resident advisor at the Superintendency of Financial Services (SFS) from 2012-2014. During that period, the advisor assisted the SFS and the Ministry of Finance (MOF) to design and issue a variety of legal frameworks critical to expanding access, including: a Financial Inclusion law; an E-Money Issuer law; a Correspondent Agent Banks circular; a Retail Bank License circular; and a Simplified Savings Account circular. Recently, the Uruguayan National Development Agency (ANDE) asked OTA to provide assistance on an intermittent basis. OTA will assist ANDE in designing relevant incentives for increasing MSMEs financial access within a sound regulatory framework. Work will focus on strengthening the National Guarantees System, implementing secured transaction reform, establishing seed capital funds, and facilitating easier access for MSMEs to the Uruguayan capital market. This work will commence in the second quarter of 2018..</narrative>
  </description>
